    "hypothesis": "H-APART-1 (BHGC-3): Laplace-Harmonic Gravity-Vector Divergence (Band 18, Band 11), Depth-Invariant Magnetic Tilt Zero-Crossing Wall, Multi-Scale Piedmont-Horst Bedrock Contact Spine & PU-Safe 89-Ch/76-Ch Dual-Cover Hydrothermal-Vent OOF with Axial-Crest Submodular Emission",
    "mechanism": "Applies exact Laplace-Harmonic horizontal divergence div(Band 18, Band 11) = -d^2g/dz^2 and Blakely-Simpson cross-contact inflection along the native horizontal gravity gradient vector coupled with basement throw ||grad(Band 15)||, Miller-Singh magnetic tilt zero-crossing wall (Band 6/3/9), multi-scale Band 12/19 piedmont-horst bedrock ridges, geodetic/seismic accommodation bridges (Bands 4,7,8,10,16), and MT clay-cap lateral edges (Band 17) + 4-block GeoDAWN 214Bi radon + GDR #1391 thermal vents. Trains a PU-safe collar-hardened Dual-Cover HistGradientBoostingClassifier OOF ensemble (89-ch M_Full inside 75.37% 1m LiDAR + 76-ch M_Sub inside the 24.63% LiDAR gap) fused with an LLI-calibrated collar-depletion attenuator and a distance-balanced far-field structural-geothermal spine floor, emitted via axial-crest submodular greedy CELF (K=37,654, B=2.0 px, min_sep_px=3.22).",
